whose measures have a sum of $90^\\circ,$ a right angle.\n\n![](images/27/2723049c087f5fa7b061bc9f1d4fb8c894c1e94aee3dfb994a237cd889a377e0.png)\n\nFor example, the angles in the diagram above are complementary because the sum of their measures is $90^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n60^\\circ +30^\\circ = 90^\\circ\n$$" 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186116445 1065 2192 13194139535590 17592186045417 false] [17592186116445 1065 13548 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520622 1058 #edb/ref 17592186116387 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520622 1061 619142 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520622 1062 #uuid "70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520622 1063 #edb/ref 17592186520624 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520623 1058 #edb/ref 17592186520622 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520623 1061 484814 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520623 1062 #uuid "fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520623 1063 #edb/ref 17592186503647 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520624 1064 "Now, consider the following diagram.\n\n![](images/02/02d8744bbc39ac9ed10d276071599f9008185023ebdfc3aaf97aebd498d82629.png)\n\nLet's solve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\nFrom the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n46^\\circ + (8x + 4^\\circ) = 90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{46}^{∘}+(8x+{4}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={40}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520624 1065 15157 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520624 1066 #uuid "62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" 13194139535590 17592186045417 true] [17592186520624 1067 "Working With Diagrams" 13194139535590 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" 17592186520622 "step-fab99fb7-13ba-5